{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want one connection for the whole conversation, not one request per message. Use the built-in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSocket()"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter. It opens one socket for the conversation. If a durable run drops, it reconnects automatically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-connect-from-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Connect from the client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, webSocket } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst connection = webSocket(\"/api/chat-ws\");\n\nconst { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection });","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-accept-the-socket-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Accept the socket on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Cloudflare Workers or Durable Objects, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toWebSocketResponse"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, memoryStream, toWebSocketResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(request: Request): Response {\n    return toWebSocketResponse(request, {\n      durability: (ctx) => memoryStream(ctx.request),\n      onRun: ({ messages, threadId, runId }) =>\n        chat({\n          adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n          messages,\n          threadId,\n          runId,\n        }),\n    });\n  },\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On other hosts, such as Node, accept the socket yourself. Then pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toWebSocketStream"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../resumable-streams/websockets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable Streams: WebSockets"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for this setup, the wire protocol, and the reconnect details."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To use your own wire format or a server that you do not control, write a custom adapter. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom#persistent-transports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send two messages. Both replies stream over the same socket."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-connect-from-the-client","text":"1. Connect from the client","level":2},{"id":"2-accept-the-socket-on-the-server","text":"2. Accept the socket on the server","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want one connection for the whole conversation, not one request per message. Use the built-in `webSocket()` adapter. It opens one socket for the conversation. If a durable run drops, it reconnects automatically.\n\n## 1. Connect from the client\n\n```typescript\nimport { useChat, webSocket } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst connection = webSocket(\"/api/chat-ws\");\n\nconst { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection });\n```\n\n## 2. Accept the socket on the server\n\nOn Cloudflare Workers or Durable Objects, use `toWebSocketResponse`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, memoryStream, toWebSocketResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(request: Request): Response {\n    return toWebSocketResponse(request, {\n      durability: (ctx) => memoryStream(ctx.request),\n      onRun: ({ messages, threadId, runId }) =>\n        chat({\n          adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n          messages,\n          threadId,\n          runId,\n        }),\n    });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nOn other hosts, such as Node, accept the socket yourself. Then pass it to `toWebSocketStream`. See [Resumable Streams: WebSockets](../resumable-streams/websockets) for this setup, the wire protocol, and the reconnect details.\n\nTo use your own wire format or a server that you do not control, write a custom adapter. See [Custom Transports](./custom#persistent-transports).\n\nSend two messages. Both replies stream over the same socket.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: WebSockets\nid: transports-websockets\norder: 4\ndescription: \"Run many chat turns over one resumable WebSocket with the webSocket() adapter and toWebSocketResponse or toWebSocketStream on the server.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - websocket\n  - webSocket\n  - toWebSocketResponse\n  - toWebSocketStream\n  - persistent transport\n  - resumable websocket\n---\n\nYou want one connection for the whole conversation, not one request per message. Use the built-in `webSocket()` adapter. It opens one socket for the conversation. If a durable run drops, it reconnects automatically.\n\n## 1. Connect from the client\n\n```typescript\nimport { useChat, webSocket } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst connection = webSocket(\"/api/chat-ws\");\n\nconst { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection });\n```\n\n## 2. Accept the socket on the server\n\nOn Cloudflare Workers or Durable Objects, use `toWebSocketResponse`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, memoryStream, toWebSocketResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(request: Request): Response {\n    return toWebSocketResponse(request, {\n      durability: (ctx) => memoryStream(ctx.request),\n      onRun: ({ messages, threadId, runId }) =>\n        chat({\n          adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n          messages,\n          threadId,\n          runId,\n        }),\n    });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nOn other hosts, such as Node, accept the socket yourself. Then pass it to `toWebSocketStream`. See [Resumable Streams: WebSockets](../resumable-streams/websockets) for this setup, the wire protocol, and the reconnect details.\n\nTo use your own wire format or a server that you do not control, write a custom adapter. See [Custom Transports](./custom#persistent-transports).\n\nSend two messages. Both replies stream over the same socket.\n"}
